 "methods_note": "Full-shard censuses, exact shares, no CIs. Sorted by (run_id,step) mergesort. ent_file/ent_path are integer counts (not filenames) and tb2 file_shown is always empty, so file identity = normalized non-empty targets_str only. Denominators stated per metric. Chain adjacency = STRICT (same run, equal sig, step increments by exactly 1). Consecutive-row adjacency was tested and REJECTED: it gives 47.36% TB2 ge2 runs, exceeding the prior-round 42.6% ceiling; strict reproduces prior 42.6% exactly (6284/14750). Duplicate step indices exist in tb2 (e.g. 0,0,1,1,...), hence the gap. nebius steps are unique per run (both variants agree). Prior static-output subset (15.6% runs/4.3% steps) and sleep chains (1.2% runs) use narrower sub-definitions and were not exactly reproduced (strict static-ge2 = 19.1%/5.3%; strict sleep-ge2 all-sleep chains = 0.73% runs); all len>=3 categorized cuts in this census fall far below every ceiling. Test-flavored = is_test==1 OR lowercased cmd_family in {pytest,unittest,npm test,make,gradle,go test,cargo test}. Theater error signal = st_error>=1 OR st_exit not in (-999,0); in practice st_error is N/A(-1) and the footprint is driven by st_exit. Desert long-run threshold uses the literal n_steps column (>=20).",
